How to Prevent Sanitary Pad Leakage During Your Period

Sanitary pad leakage can be frustrating, especially when you are at school, work, travelling, or sleeping. However, several simple steps can reduce the possibility of leaks and make period days more comfortable.

One of the most important factors is choosing a pad that matches your menstrual flow. If your flow is heavy, a small or low-absorbency pad may become saturated quickly. In that situation, choosing a longer or higher-absorbency pad can provide better protection.

Pad length is especially important during heavy-flow days. A longer pad provides greater front-to-back coverage and may reduce the chance of menstrual fluid reaching the edges.

For nighttime use, an overnight pad can be helpful. Since you may remain in the same position for several hours, additional coverage can provide greater peace of mind.

Correct positioning is also important. Place the pad in the centre of your underwear and make sure it is securely attached. If the pad has wings, fold them around the sides of the underwear.

Your underwear can also affect pad performance. Choose underwear that fits securely and provides a stable surface for the pad. Very loose underwear may allow the pad to move.

Changing your pad regularly is another important step. Do not wait until the pad is completely saturated. Check it periodically and replace it when necessary.

Heavy-flow days may require more frequent changes than lighter days. Understanding your own menstrual pattern can help you decide when to change your pad.

Physical activity can also affect pad positioning. If you are walking for long periods, exercising, or travelling, make sure your pad is properly positioned before starting the activity.

