If you experience frequent leakage despite choosing an appropriate pad and changing it regularly, consider whether your menstrual flow may be unusually heavy. Repeatedly soaking through pads may be a reason to speak with a healthcare professional.

Accidental leaks can happen to anyone, so there is no need to feel embarrassed. Keeping spare pads and underwear in your bag can help you handle unexpected situations calmly.

The best way to prevent leaks is to combine the right pad size, suitable absorbency, proper positioning, regular changes, and preparation. These simple habits can make period management much easier.
